// "Adrift": a cue for the opening scene.
//
// What it is for. The opening (scenes/opening), read from three stills of it: a grey, overcast
// sea in long slow swells; one small figure in a skiff under a ribbed sail; sea stacks standing
// off; and far away a rock hanging in the sky with a cathedral on it, the one place to go. The
// quiet before anything happens. The music is the boat for a minute, and the rock for half of one.
//
// Mood: alone, vast, drawn onward.
//
// Tempo and feel. A slow six: written as bars of three quarter notes at 186, heard as pairs of
// bars (one swell, 1.9 s). Nothing swings; every note is on a beat.
//
// Key. F minor, natural. No dominant anywhere.
//
// The spine, from the listener's taste sheet: "the patient drone" (devices 9, 4 and 6), with the
// band withheld (1), the same material made heavy (2) and the cut as the resolution (3).
//   4: a rolling figure is the bed, F3 and C4 that never change and one note over them that
//      moves once a swell, with an echo two beats behind so it rolls three against two.
//   9: for 46 s there is the figure and a bell, and nothing else.
//   6: the tune hovers on two neighbouring notes, each struck long then short, and is held.
//   1, 2: no bass and no drums until 0:47; then both on one downbeat, under the same tune.
//   3: the chorus ends on D flat with the tune's F held over the bar line; the cut to the
//      figure alone makes that F the home note.
//
// The one bold thing. Until the chorus the piece stands on F. When the bass arrives it goes
// straight down to D flat under the tune's same C, which turns from a fifth into a major
// seventh: the floor drops away, as the rock hangs. Everything round that is plain.
//
// The hook (this take's; the notes below say how it got here) is the listener's own, hummed:
// the rocking phrase lands on A flat, then on G; a walk down from E flat lands on A flat again;
// a long G waits; and a two-note pickup carries every phrase into the next.
//
// An ear's notes on the second take (which had a clarinet tune, a bowed drone under the verses,
// and a tune whose third and fourth phrases climbed to F and walked down): "the drop at 46 is
// fire, and the first melody kills, but then you ruin it by wandering. I want the same melody
// line, but then the last note to be different (resolved)." The lead synth should be "much
// richer and sweeter and harmonic". Before the chorus the clarinet "is the wrong instrument";
// the bell that played the first phrase in the intro "is actually much better on its own"; and
// the drone in the background "is ruining the atmosphere". So, in this take: the tune is the
// one phrase with a changing last note; the bell carries it before the chorus; the clarinet and
// every held string before the chorus are gone; the lead is a unison of five with a second
// voice a third under it.
//
// Palette, each with a job:
//   figure    a plucked synth, echoed: the water. Never stops but for one bar.
//   keys      electric piano, high and soft, echoed: the tune before the chorus, answers in it,
//             the tune again after it.
//   lead      a unison synth, one voice: the tune in the chorus; a second like it a third under.
//   violin    a third over the tune, late: the last half of the last chorus. Else a held A flat.
//   wall      two driven synths, left and right, roots and fifths, striking the tune's rhythm.
//   pad, viola   F, A flat and C held under the wall; the bass under them changes what they are.
//   sub, round, cello   the bass, withheld: a sine, its line an octave up, and a bowed octave.
//   kit       bass drum, snare and clap, hat, one crash: a slow six.
//
// Form (bars of three; energy 1 to 10):
//    1-16   intro    1  the figure alone; the bell tries the tune's first notes
//   17-32   verse 1  2  the bell says the round
//   33-48   verse 2  3  the same in octaves; bar 48 is empty but the lead's two-note pickup
//   49-64   chorus 1 8  everything, on the downbeat: F minor and D flat, twice round
//   65-80   chorus 2 9  the same; the violin a third over the tune from bar 73
//   81-96   outro    2  cut on the bar line to the figure; the lead's F hangs over into it; the
//                       bell says the phrase twice more, ending home
//
// An ear's notes on the third take (one phrase said four times, ending G, A flat, G, F over
// F minor and D flat; the bell teasing the phrase's first notes in the intro; no strings before
// the chorus): the bell's notes at the beginning "are a bit odd. They're like partial phrases."
// "Maybe a cello in the beginning to fill out the soundscape would be cool, playing some
// chords. Then switching to the electronic synth vibe on the chorus is cool." And: "musically
// it's very close but it's missing that killer melodic hook and resolution vibe." So, in this
// take: the round's chords are F minor, D flat, E flat, F minor, a real way home; the hook is
// the phrase twice (hanging on G, then on A flat), then an answer that leaps to E flat and
// falls in even notes, C, B flat, A flat, G, onto F as F minor arrives, and holds it. The bell
// says only whole rounds. Cello and viola play the chords' roots and fifths from the first bar.
//
// An ear's notes on the fourth take, sent as a voice memo with three hums (their pitches read
// by a tracker and played back to check; the words between them typed afterwards):
//   The main melody, hummed in the piece's key ("my fix for the main melody"): the rocking
//   phrase landing on a long A flat; again landing on G; then E flat, D flat, C, B flat walking
//   down to a long A flat; then a long G. A two-note pickup, A flat and B flat, ties each phrase
//   to the next.
//   The opening line (the figure) should "not have 4 phrases, but instead alternate between the
//   first two".
//   "A twinkly synth in the background on the chorus for some texture/flavor": a quick rise to
//   a held high E flat.
// So, in this take: the tune is the hummed one, note for note. The chords under it are chosen
// to fit it: F minor, E flat, A flat, E flat (the walk-down lands on A flat's root; the long G
// is E flat's third, and the pickup carries it home to F minor). The last G falls to F on the
// cut. The figure has only its A flat and G patterns, ordered so its top note agrees with the
// note the tune is holding. The bell plays the rise to E flat as each phrase lands, in the
// chorus.
//
// And after the fifth take: "instead of the droning synth in the beginning, some piano chords
// could be nice." The bowed cello and viola before the chorus and after it are gone (they stay
// in the chorus); an electric piano strikes the chords there, once a swell, a root with a fifth
// and a tenth over it.
//
// And after the sixth: the piano chords "are nice and it's what I want, but they're way too
// quiet"; the twinkle "is too quiet too, and I'd like the twinkle to be separate flourishes";
// "the mix is a bit muddy overall"; and "in the rise of the chorus, I want a violin to come in
// with its own phrase to expound on the main melody. Something mournful." So: the piano is up
// and voiced as triads in the middle of the keyboard; the twinkle is its own synth, five
// flourishes no two alike (the hummed rise first); the cello and viola are gone, and the one
// bowed instrument is a violin that enters with the last chorus and moves where the tune holds;
// the middle is thinned (higher cuts, less sent to the room and the echo).
//
// And after the seventh: "I liked the bigger drop. Violin is not loud enough. We should cut
// the second lower toned bell that overlays the first one. Opening phrases should rotate on
// the 2s not on the 4s. Half as many twinkle embellishments. I would change the electric piano
// to the grand piano." So: the chorus is up and the verses are no louder; the violin is up;
// the bell is one line in both verses; the figure changes every two bars before the chorus and
// after it (in the chorus it stays with the tune's long notes, four bars each); two flourishes,
// one a chorus; and the chords are on the engine's grand (engine::session's `piano`, added for
// this).
//
// And after the eighth (grand piano chords, a bowed violin): "a lot of the best sounds are the
// outright synths rather than the sampled instruments. Maybe we should lean into synths and
// beats for the soundtrack?" So this take is synths, the bell and the kit: the chords are a
// struck synth that blooms and fades, and the violin's line is a singing synth lead. Take
// eight's source is kept beside its render (build/adrift/song-v8.wrela) to compare.
//
// Not heard by its writer. What was measured is in the hand-off, not here.

use engine::drum::{CLAP, CRASH, Drum, HAT, KICK, SNARE}
use engine::pattern::{Feel, Pattern, pattern, struck, swung, tacet}
use engine::perform::{Mark, Performance, Taste, bar, perform}
use engine::score::{Meter, Score, meter, score}
use engine::session::{Master, Session, Strip, session}
use engine::synth::{PAD, PLUCK, Patch, SOAR, SUB}
use engine::tine::{SUITCASE, Tine}
use engine::tone::Shape

pub const TITLE: Text = "Adrift"
pub const TEMPO: f32 = 186.0
pub const BARS: u32 = 96

fn three() -> Meter {
    meter(beats: 3, unit: 4)
}

fn part(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Score {
    score(TITLE, three()).voice(name, lines)
}

fn rests(name: Text, bars: u32) -> Score {
    var s = part(name, ["r/2. |"])
    for _i in 1..bars {
        s = (take s).then(part(name, ["r/2. |"]))
    }
    s
}

fn played(s: Score, taste: Taste, feel: Feel) -> Performance {
    swung(perform(s, taste, [Mark::Hold { at: bar(1), by: 1.0 }; 0]), feel)
}

// ---- the figure: F3 and C4 fixed, and over them A flat or G ------------------------------------

const FA: Text = "f3/4 c4 ab4 |"
const FG: Text = "f3/4 c4 g4 |"

/// The figure before the chorus and after it: A flat for one swell (two bars), G for the next.
fn rolling(first: Text) -> Score {
    part("figure", [first, FA, FG, FG, FA, FA, FG, FG, FA, FA, FG, FG, FA, FA, FG, FG])
}

/// The figure in the chorus: the same two, four bars each, as the chords and the tune's long
/// notes go (A flat, G, A flat, G), so its top note is never a semitone from the note the lead
/// is holding in its own octave.
fn round(first: Text) -> Score {
    part("figure", [first, FA, FA, FA, FG, FG, FG, FG, FA, FA, FA, FA, FG, FG, FG, FG])
}

fn figure() -> Score {
    let verse2 = part(
        "figure",
        [
            "f3/4 !mp c4 ab4 |",
            FA,
            FG,
            FG,
            FA,
            FA,
            FG,
            FG,
            FA,
            FA,
            FG,
            FG,
            FA,
            FA,
            "f3/4 c4 r/4 |",
            "r/2. |",
        ],
    )
    let outro = part(
        "figure",
        [
            "f3/4 !mp c4 ab4 |",
            FA,
            FG,
            FG,
            FA,
            FA,
            FG,
            FG,
            FA,
            FA,
            FG,
            FG,
            "f3/4 !p c4 ab4 | f3/4 c4 r/4 | f3/2. ~ | f3/2. |",
        ],
    )
    rolling("f3/4 !mp c4 ab4 |")
        .then(rolling("f3/4 !mp c4 ab4 |"))
        .then(verse2)
        .then(round("f3/4 !mf c4 ab4 |"))
        .then(round("f3/4 !mf c4 ab4 |"))
        .then(outro)
}

// ---- the tune, as hummed -----------------------------------------------------------------------

const T1: Text = "c5/2 c5/4 | bb4/2 ( c5/4 ) | ab4/2. ~ | ab4/4 ab4/4 bb4/4 |"
const T2: Text = "c5/2 c5/4 | bb4/2 ( c5/4 ) | g4/2. ~ | g4/4 ab4/4 bb4/4 |"
const T3: Text = "eb5/2 ( db5/4 | c5/2 bb4/4 ) | ab4/2. ~ | ab4/4 ab4/4 bb4/4 |"
const T4: Text = "g4/2. ~ | g4/2. ~ | g4/2. | r/4 ab4/4 bb4/4 |"
/// The last: the G falls to F on the cut, and the F hangs into the outro.
const T4_CUT: Text = "g4/2. ~ | g4/2. ~ | g4/2. ~ | g4/2. | f4/2. ~ | f4/2. |"

fn lead() -> Score {
    rests("lead", bars: 47)
        .then(part("lead", ["r/4 ab4/4 !mf bb4/4 |", T1, T2, T3, T4]))
        .then(part("lead", [T1, T2, T3, T4_CUT]))
        .then(rests("lead", bars: 14))
}

// A second voice under it: thirds, or the chord's own note where a third would be outside it.
const U1: Text = "ab4/2 ab4/4 | f4/2 ( ab4/4 ) | f4/2. ~ | f4/4 r/2 |"
const U2: Text = "g4/2 g4/4 | g4/2 g4/4 | eb4/2. ~ | eb4/4 r/2 |"
const U3: Text = "c5/2 ( bb4/4 ) | ab4/2. | eb4/2. ~ | eb4/4 r/2 |"
const U4: Text = "eb4/2. ~ | eb4/2. ~ | eb4/2. | r/2. |"

fn under() -> Score {
    rests("under", bars: 48)
        .then(
            part("under", ["ab4/2 !mp ab4/4 | f4/2 ( ab4/4 ) | f4/2. ~ | f4/4 r/2 |", U2, U3, U4]),
        )
        .then(part("under", [U1, U2, U3, U4]))
        .then(rests("under", bars: 16))
}

// ---- the bell: the tune before the chorus, the hummed rise to E flat in it, the way home after -

const K1: Text = "c6/2 c6/4 | bb5/2 c6/4 | ab5/2. ~ | ab5/4 ab5/4 bb5/4 |"
const K2: Text = "c6/2 c6/4 | bb5/2 c6/4 | g5/2. ~ | g5/4 ab5/4 bb5/4 |"
const K3: Text = "eb6/2 db6/4 | c6/2 bb5/4 | ab5/2. ~ | ab5/4 ab5/4 bb5/4 |"
const K4: Text = "g5/2. ~ | g5/2. | r/2. | r/4 ab5/4 bb5/4 |"
const K4_END: Text = "g5/2. ~ | g5/2. | r/2. | r/2. |"

fn keys() -> Score {
    rests("keys", bars: 15)
        .then(part("keys", ["r/4 ab5/4 !mf bb5/4 |", K1, K2, K3, K4]))
        .then(part("keys", [K1, K2, K3, K4_END]))
        .then(rests("keys", bars: 32))
        .then(
            part(
                "keys",
                [
                    "r/2. | r/2. | r/2. | r/2. |",
                    "eb6/2 !mp db6/4 | c6/2 bb5/4 | ab5/2. ~ | ab5/2. |",
                    "g5/2. ~ | g5/2. ~ | g5/2. | r/2. |",
                    "f5/2. ~ | f5/2. | f6/2. !p | r/2. |",
                ],
            ),
        )
}

// ---- the twinkle: two flourishes high over the chorus, one in each ----------------------------

const QUIET: Text = "r/2. | r/2. | r/2. | r/2. |"
/// The hummed one: two quick notes up to a held E flat.
const FL_RISE: Text = "r/2. | r/2 c6/8 !mf db6/8 | eb6/2. | r/2. |"
/// One that falls, through E flat's chord.
const FL_FALL: Text = "r/2. | r/4 eb6/8 c6/8 bb5/8 g5/8 | eb5/2. | r/2. |"

fn twinkle() -> Score {
    rests("twinkle", bars: 48)
        .then(part("twinkle", [FL_RISE, QUIET, QUIET, QUIET]))
        .then(part("twinkle", [QUIET, FL_FALL, QUIET, QUIET]))
        .then(rests("twinkle", bars: 16))
}

// ---- the cry: a second voice's own phrase over the last chorus, moving where the tune holds --------------

fn violin() -> Score {
    rests("violin", bars: 64)
        .then(
            part(
                "violin",
                [
                    // Over F minor: a held A flat, then a fall from C as the tune rests on its A flat.
                    "ab5/2. !mf ~ | ab5/2. | c6/2 ( bb5/4 ) | ab5/2 ( g5/4 ) |",
                    // Over E flat: G held, then a sigh down from B flat.
                    "g5/2. ~ | g5/2. | bb5/2 ( ab5/4 ) | g5/2 ( f5/4 ) |",
                    // Over A flat: up against the tune's walk down, to its one high E flat.
                    "ab5/2. | bb5/2. | c6/2 ( eb6/4 | db6/2 c6/4 ) |",
                    // Over the tune's long G: B flat down by step to E flat.
                    "bb5/2 ( ab5/4 ) | g5/2 ( f5/4 ) | eb5/2. ~ | eb5/2. |",
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(rests("violin", bars: 16))
}

// ---- the glow: the chords before the chorus and after it, struck once a swell -----------------

// A root in the left hand; the triad in the middle of the keyboard in the right.
const PR_F: Text = "<ab3 c4 f4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. |"
const PL_F: Text = "f2/2. ~ | f2/2. | f2/2. ~ | f2/2. |"
const PR_EB: Text = "<g3 bb3 eb4>/2. ~ | <g3 bb3 eb4>/2. | <g3 bb3 eb4>/2. ~ | <g3 bb3 eb4>/2. |"
const PL_EB: Text = "eb2/2. ~ | eb2/2. | eb2/2. ~ | eb2/2. |"
const PR_AB: Text = "<ab3 c4 eb4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 eb4>/2. | <ab3 c4 eb4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 eb4>/2. |"
const PL_AB: Text = "ab2/2. ~ | ab2/2. | ab2/2. ~ | ab2/2. |"
const PR_EB_END: Text = "<g3 bb3 eb4>/2. ~ | <g3 bb3 eb4>/2. | <g3 bb3 eb4>/2. | r/2. |"
const PL_EB_END: Text = "eb2/2. ~ | eb2/2. | eb2/2. | r/2. |"
const PR_F_END: Text = "<ab3 c4 f4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. |"

fn hands(right: [Text], left: [Text]) -> Score {
    score(TITLE, three()).voice("piano", right).voice("left", left)
}

fn piano() -> Score {
    var quiet = hands(["r/2. |"], ["r/2. |"])
    for _i in 1..32 {
        quiet = (take quiet).then(hands(["r/2. |"], ["r/2. |"]))
    }
    hands(
        [
            "<ab3 c4 f4>/2. !mp ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. |",
            PR_EB,
            PR_AB,
            PR_EB,
        ],
        [PL_F, PL_EB, PL_AB, PL_EB],
    )
        .then(hands([PR_F, PR_EB, PR_AB, PR_EB], [PL_F, PL_EB, PL_AB, PL_EB]))
        .then(hands([PR_F, PR_EB, PR_AB, PR_EB_END], [PL_F, PL_EB, PL_AB, PL_EB_END]))
        .then(quiet)
        .then(
            hands(
                [
                    "<ab3 c4 f4>/2. !mp ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4 f4>/2. |",
                    PR_AB,
                    PR_EB,
                    PR_F_END,
                ],
                [PL_F, PL_AB, PL_EB, PL_F],
            ),
        )
}

// ---- the chorus's band: pad, wall, bass --------------------------------------------------------

// Each chord without the note the second voice holds over it.
const PD_F: Text = "<f3 ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <f3 ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <f3 ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <f3 ab3 c4>/2. |"
const PD_EB: Text = "<g3 bb3>/2. ~ | <g3 bb3>/2. ~ | <g3 bb3>/2. ~ | <g3 bb3>/2. |"
const PD_AB: Text = "<ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <ab3 c4>/2. |"

fn pad() -> Score {
    rests("pad", bars: 48)
        .then(
            part(
                "pad",
                [
                    "<f3 ab3 c4>/2. !mp ~ | <f3 ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <f3 ab3 c4>/2. ~ | <f3 ab3 c4>/2. |",
                    PD_EB,
                    PD_AB,
                    PD_EB,
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(part("pad", [PD_F, PD_EB, PD_AB, PD_EB]))
        .then(rests("pad", bars: 16))
}

// The wall strikes the tune's own rhythm: long, then long and short.
const W_F: Text = "<f2 c3 f3>/2. | <f2 c3 f3>/2 <f2 c3 f3>/4 | <f2 c3 f3>/2. | <f2 c3 f3>/2 <f2 c3 f3>/4 |"
const W_EB: Text = "<eb3 bb3>/2. | <eb3 bb3>/2 <eb3 bb3>/4 | <eb3 bb3>/2. | <eb3 bb3>/2 <eb3 bb3>/4 |"
const W_AB: Text = "<ab2 eb3 ab3>/2. | <ab2 eb3 ab3>/2 <ab2 eb3 ab3>/4 | <ab2 eb3 ab3>/2. | <ab2 eb3 ab3>/2 <ab2 eb3 ab3>/4 |"
const W_EB_END: Text = "<eb3 bb3>/2. | <eb3 bb3>/2 <eb3 bb3>/4 | <eb3 bb3>/2. | <eb3 bb3>/2. |"

fn wall() -> Score {
    rests("wall", bars: 48)
        .then(
            part(
                "wall",
                [
                    "<f2 c3 f3>/2. !mf | <f2 c3 f3>/2 <f2 c3 f3>/4 | <f2 c3 f3>/2. | <f2 c3 f3>/2 <f2 c3 f3>/4 |",
                    W_EB,
                    W_AB,
                    W_EB,
                ],
            ),
        )
        .then(part("wall", [W_F, W_EB, W_AB, W_EB_END]))
        .then(rests("wall", bars: 16))
}

const B_F: Text = "f1/2. | f1/2 f1/4 | f1/2. | f1/2 f1/4 |"
const B_EB: Text = "eb1/2. | eb1/2 eb1/4 | eb1/2. | eb1/2 eb1/4 |"
const B_AB: Text = "ab1/2. | ab1/2 ab1/4 | ab1/2. | ab1/2 g1/4 |"
const B_EB_UP: Text = "eb1/2. | eb1/2 eb1/4 | eb1/2. | eb1/4 eb1/4 eb1/4 |"
const B_EB_END: Text = "eb1/2. | eb1/2 eb1/4 | eb1/2. | eb1/2. |"

fn sub() -> Score {
    rests("sub", bars: 48)
        .then(part("sub", ["f1/2. !mf | f1/2 f1/4 | f1/2. | f1/2 f1/4 |", B_EB, B_AB, B_EB_UP]))
        .then(part("sub", [B_F, B_EB, B_AB, B_EB_END]))
        .then(rests("sub", bars: 16))
}

const O_F: Text = "f2/2. | f2/2 f2/4 | f2/2. | f2/2 f2/4 |"
const O_EB: Text = "eb2/2. | eb2/2 eb2/4 | eb2/2. | eb2/2 eb2/4 |"
const O_AB: Text = "ab2/2. | ab2/2 ab2/4 | ab2/2. | ab2/2 g2/4 |"
const O_EB_UP: Text = "eb2/2. | eb2/2 eb2/4 | eb2/2. | eb2/4 eb2/4 eb2/4 |"
const O_EB_END: Text = "eb2/2. | eb2/2 eb2/4 | eb2/2. | eb2/2. |"

fn over() -> Score {
    rests("round", bars: 48)
        .then(part("round", ["f2/2. !mf | f2/2 f2/4 | f2/2. | f2/2 f2/4 |", O_EB, O_AB, O_EB_UP]))
        .then(part("round", [O_F, O_EB, O_AB, O_EB_END]))
        .then(rests("round", bars: 16))
}

// ---- the kit: twelve steps to a bar of three; one swell is two bars ----------------------------

fn drum(name: Text, lines: [Text]) -> Pattern {
    pattern(name, three(), lines, steps: 12)
}

/// A chorus's sixteen bars of one drum: three swells of `a` and one of `b`, then three of `a`
/// and one of `c`.
fn chorus_of(name: Text, a: Text, b: Text, c: Text) -> Pattern {
    drum(name, [a, a, a, b, a, a, a, c])
}

fn kick() -> Pattern {
    let a = "X... .... .... | .... .... x... |"
    let b = "X... .... x... | .... .... x... |"
    let c = "X... .... x... | .... x... x... |"
    let last = "X... .... x... | .... .... .... |"
    tacet(three(), bars: 48)
        .then(chorus_of("kick", a, b, c))
        .then(chorus_of("kick", a, b, last))
        .then(tacet(three(), bars: 16))
}

fn snare() -> Pattern {
    let a = ".... .... .... | X... .... .... |"
    let b = ".... .... .... | X... .... ..o. |"
    let c = ".... .... .... | X... ..o. .... |"
    tacet(three(), bars: 48)
        .then(chorus_of("snare", a, b, c))
        .then(chorus_of("snare", a, b, a))
        .then(tacet(three(), bars: 16))
}

fn clap() -> Pattern {
    let a = ".... .... .... | x... .... .... |"
    tacet(three(), bars: 48)
        .then(chorus_of("clap", a, a, a))
        .then(chorus_of("clap", a, a, a))
        .then(tacet(three(), bars: 16))
}

fn hat() -> Pattern {
    let a = "X.o. x.o. x.o. | x.o. x.o. x.o. |"
    let b = "X.o. x.o. x.o. | x.o. x.o. x.x. |"
    tacet(three(), bars: 48)
        .then(chorus_of("hat", a, b, b))
        .then(chorus_of("hat", a, b, a))
        .then(tacet(three(), bars: 16))
}

fn crash() -> Pattern {
    let hit = drum("crash", ["X... .... .... |"])
    tacet(three(), bars: 48)
        .then(hit.clone())
        .then(tacet(three(), bars: 15))
        .then(hit)
        .then(tacet(three(), bars: 31))
}

// ---- the sounds --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The figure: a pluck that rings a little longer than the engine's, and opens less.
const WATER: Patch = Patch {
    cutoff: 900.0,
    open: 3.6,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.001, decay: 0.3, sustain: 0.1, release: 0.3 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.002, decay: 0.9, sustain: 0.18, release: 0.4 },
    ..PLUCK,
}

/// The chorus's tune: five sawtooths and pulses a few cents apart over a triangle, one voice,
/// barely driven, its filter low and round; it slides under a slur and its vibrato comes late.
const SUNG: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.5,
    pulse: 0.25,
    width: 0.45,
    pwm: 0.08,
    pwm_hz: 0.6,
    triangle: 0.15,
    unison: 5,
    detune: 18.0,
    wide: 0.55,
    drift: 3.0,
    glide: 0.07,
    vibrato: 12.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.2,
    vibrato_wake: 0.3,
    cutoff: 2400.0,
    open: 1.8,
    q: 0.75,
    follow: 0.3,
    touch: 0.5,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.03, decay: 0.5, sustain: 0.65, release: 0.3 },
    push: 0.5,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.03, decay: 0.6, sustain: 0.9, release: 0.3 },
    drive: 0.4,
    range_db: 12.0,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.45,
}

/// The wall: sawtooth and pulse, driven, dark.
const WALL: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.5,
    pulse: 0.3,
    width: 0.45,
    spread: 9.0,
    wide: 0.3,
    cutoff: 1100.0,
    open: 1.8,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.3,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.01, decay: 0.6, sustain: 0.5, release: 0.3 },
    push: 1.0,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.01, decay: 0.8, sustain: 0.8, release: 0.25 },
    drive: 1.6,
    level: 0.25,
}

/// The bass's audible octave.
const ROUND: Patch = Patch {
    triangle: 0.6,
    sine: 0.5,
    saw: 0.2,
    cutoff: 420.0,
    open: 1.4,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 0.5, sustain: 0.3, release: 0.15 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.006, decay: 1.2, sustain: 0.5, release: 0.12 },
    drive: 1.2,
    voices: 1,
    level: 0.5,
}

const HELD: Patch = Patch { cutoff: 700.0, ..PAD }

/// The keys: a little more bell, a slower sway.
const LIGHT: Tine = Tine { bell: 0.2, tremolo: 0.35, tremolo_hz: 3.1, ..SUITCASE }

/// The twinkle: a sine and a triangle that ring and fade, a little pulse for an edge.
const GLINT: Patch = Patch {
    sine: 0.7,
    triangle: 0.4,
    pulse: 0.08,
    width: 0.3,
    cutoff: 6000.0,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.001, decay: 0.7, sustain: 0.12, release: 0.8 },
    range_db: 10.0,
    voices: 6,
    level: 0.35,
}

/// The chords: a struck synth that blooms and fades, three sawtooths and pulses apart over a
/// triangle, its filter closing as it rings.
const GLOW: Patch = Patch {
    saw: 0.35,
    pulse: 0.2,
    width: 0.45,
    pwm: 0.1,
    pwm_hz: 0.5,
    triangle: 0.3,
    unison: 3,
    detune: 12.0,
    wide: 0.7,
    drift: 2.0,
    cutoff: 700.0,
    open: 2.6,
    q: 0.8,
    follow: 0.4,
    touch: 0.6,
    filter: Shape { attack: 0.004, decay: 1.3, sustain: 0.35, release: 0.9 },
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.006, decay: 1.8, sustain: 0.45, release: 1.0 },
    range_db: 12.0,
    level: 0.3,
}

/// The second chorus's own voice: the engine's high lead, slower to speak and to let go, with
/// more vibrato, sliding where its line is slurred.
const CRY: Patch = Patch {
    glide: 0.09,
    vibrato: 18.0,
    vibrato_hz: 5.6,
    vibrato_wake: 0.22,
    cutoff: 2000.0,
    amp: Shape { attack: 0.03, decay: 0.5, sustain: 0.9, release: 0.3 },
    ..SOAR,
}

/// A crash whose hits come out alike.
const SPLASH: Drum = Drum { restless: 0.3, ..CRASH }

pub fn build() -> Session {
    var s = session(
        TEMPO,
        Master {
            gain: 4.0,
            glue_db: -16.0,
            glue: 0.3,
            makeup: 3.0,
            warmth: 1.0,
            ceiling: -1.0,
            room_time: 1.7,
            room_size: 1.7,
            room_db: -5.0,
            room_wait: 0.03,
            room_low_cut: 300.0,
            echo_beats: 2.0,
            echo_again: 0.42,
            echo_hz: 2000.0,
            echo_db: -5.0,
            duck_time: 0.16,
        },
        beats: 3,
    )
    let straight = Feel {}

    s.drum("kick", KICK, struck(kick(), TEMPO, straight, key: 36), Strip { gain: -0.5 })
    s.drum(
        "snare",
        SNARE,
        struck(snare(), TEMPO, Feel { late: 0.012, seed: 2 }, key: 38),
        Strip { gain: -10.0, low_cut: 120.0, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "clap",
        CLAP,
        struck(clap(), TEMPO, Feel { late: 0.022, seed: 3 }, key: 39),
        Strip { gain: -5.0, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.35, pan: 0.1 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "hat",
        HAT,
        struck(hat(), TEMPO, Feel { late: -0.004, uneven: 0.08, seed: 4 }, key: 42),
        Strip { gain: -2.0, low_cut: 400.0, pan: 0.4, room: 0.15 },
    )
    s.drum(
        "crash",
        SPLASH,
        struck(crash(), TEMPO, straight, key: 49),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, low_cut: 300.0, pan: -0.25, room: 0.3 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "sub",
        SUB,
        played(sub(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.04 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -5.5, high_cut: 1500.0, duck: 5.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "round",
        ROUND,
        played(over(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.04 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -11.0, low_cut: 90.0, high_cut: 2500.0, duck: 3.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "wall left",
        WALL,
        played(wall(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.06 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -4.5, pan: -0.8, low_cut: 150.0, room: 0.15, duck: 2.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "wall right",
        Patch { spread: 13.0, width: 0.38, ..WALL },
        played(wall(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.06 }, Feel { late: 0.006 }),
        Strip { gain: -4.5, pan: 0.8, low_cut: 150.0, room: 0.15, duck: 2.0 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "pad",
        HELD,
        played(pad(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, low_cut: 220.0, high_cut: 5000.0, room: 0.35 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "figure",
        WATER,
        played(figure(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.05, metre: 0.08 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -5.5, low_cut: 140.0, room: 0.25, echo: 0.35 },
    )
    s.synth(
        "lead",
        SUNG,
        played(lead(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.05, detache: 0.08 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -3.5, low_cut: 250.0, room: 0.3, echo: 0.22 },
    )

    s.synth(
        "under",
        Patch { detune: 14.0, ..SUNG },
        played(under(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.05, detache: 0.08 }, Feel { late: 0.008 }),
        Strip { gain: -9.0, low_cut: 200.0, pan: -0.15, room: 0.3, echo: 0.22 },
    )
    s.tine(
        "keys",
        LIGHT,
        played(keys(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -14.0, low_cut: 300.0, pan: 0.1, room: 0.5, echo: 0.4 },
    )

    s.synth(
        "glow",
        GLOW,
        played(piano(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02, roll: 0.014 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -8.0, low_cut: 80.0, room: 0.35, echo: 0.1 },
    )

    s.synth(
        "twinkle",
        GLINT,
        played(twinkle(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, detache: 0.02 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -7.0, low_cut: 500.0, pan: 0.3, room: 0.45, echo: 0.45 },
    )

    s.synth(
        "cry",
        CRY,
        played(violin(), Taste { tempo: TEMPO, legato: 0.06, detache: 0.04 }, straight),
        Strip { gain: -4.0, pan: 0.2, low_cut: 300.0, room: 0.35, echo: 0.25 },
    )

    s.key("kick")
    s
}
